runakefli (1.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New clickhouse.tls block (enabled, ca_file, cert_file, key_file,
    server_name, insecure_skip_verify): the native ClickHouse connection
    can use TLS, e.g. ClickHouse Cloud's port 9440; a startup warning
    fires when TLS is off and the address is not loopback.
  * The index and drilldown endpoints (index/stats, index/volume*,
    detected_labels, patterns) fan out per tenant again with
    multi_tenant_queries_enabled, as documented since 0.7.0.
  * The apt repository is signed with a new Ed25519 key; its private part
    lives only in the apt-signing GitHub environment and the maintainer's
    password store. Users must re-install the keyring, or apt reports an
    unknown signature.
  * Release workflow hardening: the docs workflow builds from reviewed
    main, and the signing job is gated by the environment's deployment
    rules (main and v* tags only).

 -- Bernd Zeimetz <bernd@bzed.de>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:25:19 +0100

runakefli (1.0.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First stable release; the documentation no longer calls Rúnakefli a
    release candidate.
  * Blocked ingestion with a non-200 status processes every stream and
    answers with block_ingestion_status_code, as Loki does.
  * Discard metrics carry retention_hours on every discard path.

